{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "America is losing its smartest people. By the \nnumbers alone, 80% of postoc researchers now  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6000,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "report they are looking for positions outside of \nthe US. The number of US researchers applying for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "positions in Europe has tripled. And just across \nthe border, applications from American scientists  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15360,
    "dDurationMs": 7440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "looking for jobs in Canada rose 41% while Canadian \nscientists looking for jobs in the US fell by 13%.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Federal agencies lost over 10,000 doctor level \nSTEM and health experts over the past year.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hospitals are now running low on skilled \npractitioners entering the field and even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31840,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in purely profit-driven enterprises. People \nlike AI researchers are rather loudly finding  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37360,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "opportunities abroad. These are also only \nthe positions that we know about. And well,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this shouldn't really be happening, right? The \nUnited States has always attracted the very best  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and brightest people to live and work here. And \nit's done that for a number of logical reasons.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52640,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We have some of the best research institutions \nand schools in the world. We have a robust funding  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57120,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "system to finance cutting edge development. And \nhonestly, the not so secret reality is that very  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 62640,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smart people can normally make a lot more money \nhere than they can anywhere else in the world.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even amongst other high-income economies, startup \nfounders, scientific researchers, academics, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "medical practitioners have typically been drawn \nto America because there are more opportunities  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77840,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to get their work funded and also to be funded for \ntheir work. Now, I know what you were thinking,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83440,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yes, obviously, a lot of this has to \ndo with things like lacks or regulations,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "over financialization, and a health care system \nthat prioritizes profits over outcomes. And well,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92800,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yeah, you would have a point. But putting aside \nthe social problems these may cause for a second,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98400,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "American pharmaceutical labs, financial firms, \nhospitals, startups, big tech, and the venture  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103120,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "capital ecosystem all genuinely present amazing \nfinancial opportunities to highly skilled people.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the thing is, none of this has really \nchanged. We still have all of the systems  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114160,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "alongside the good and bad that comes with them. \nWhat has changed, though, is that despite the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119360,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "chance to make a lot more money, smart people \nfrom across the world aren't coming in nearly  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123840,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as fast as they once did. And perhaps even \nmore worryingly, the smart people that we do  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128720,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have are moving out. It doesn't sound great, but \nperhaps this could all mean more opportunities and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134640,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "training for the people who are already here, \nright? Well, we will get to that. But also,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139520,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this raises the question of where are these people \ngoing and what are they actually taking with them?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145520,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Americans are leaving the United States at record \nlevels in large part because of divisive politics  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150960,
    "dDurationMs": 6720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and an affordability crisis. A poll from the \njournal Nature earlier this year found that 75% of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157680,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "researchers in the US are considering leaving the \ncountry. We've lost more than 15,000 scientists  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164560,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the ranks of the federal government. We're \nlosing our scientific base. New breakthroughs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 168640,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in powerful lowcost Chinese AI models are sending \nshock waves through Washington and Silicon Valley  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as Chinese companies continue to narrow the \nAI gap despite vast differences in computing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179440,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "power and financial resources. Okay, so obviously \nthe most pressing question would be to ask why is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185680,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this happening? Or rather, why is it happening \nnow? And well, yeah, while it would be easy to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191040,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "blame everything on the current state of America, \nit's worth at least acknowledging that most other  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 195200,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "countries are dealing with their own problems as \nwell. And in the grand scheme of things, we still  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199680,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have it pretty good. Especially for people at the \ntop of their respective field. And yet, people who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "theoretically have the qualifications to live and \nwork almost anywhere they want are still reversing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209360,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a very long-standing trend of gravitating to \nthe USA. And they are doing it for two reasons.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The first is that despite spending hundreds of \nbillions of dollars on R\u0026D every year, we are very  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220000,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "selective with where we actually spend it. And \noverwhelmingly, it goes to projects with a clear  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224640,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "path to return on investment. The private sector \nnow funds about 3/4 of all American research and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 230160,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "development. And even amongst what's left, federal \nagencies only fund around 40% of the country's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235200,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basic research. The problem this creates is that \nprivate for-profit companies have no incentive  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240080,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to fund the risky foundational work that doesn't \nhave a clear path to making well a profit. This  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246400,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means something like climate science, which might \nactually stand in the way of corporate profits,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hasn't been well funded compared to opportunities \nin places like Europe. Last year's White House  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "budget request for the National Ocean and \nAtmospheric Administration proposed exactly 0 for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 260880,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "climate research, which would theoretically impact \nthe ocean and the atmosphere. At the same time,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267440,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for comparison, the EU set aside almost 5 billion \nof its current 2-year research budget just for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 272720,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "climate work. For the most part, this just simply \nmeans that at least for the next few years, if a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 277840,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "climate scientist wants to continue their studies, \nthey are effectively being forced to move.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282560,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The other thing is that people in these fields are \na lot more open to moving because for better or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286960,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "worse, it's kind of a part of the job. Someone \nwho just finished a PhD in one of these fields  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is effectively eternally at the whims of research \nfunding. They kind of go where the grants go. And  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 296720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially in less profitable fields of science, \nless and less of that money is in the USA. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301920,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to play devil's advocate, maybe pursuing science \nonly when it is profitable still means we keep  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 306640,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of the research that will actually \ncontribute to economic development, right?  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 310640,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, we will get to that assumption, but even \nif it was completely true, it would still be  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 315600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very shortsighted. A lot of research doesn't \nseem profitable at first before it turns out  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that it really is. Radio astronomy was developed \nto get more accurate images of the cosmos before  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326160,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the same tech ended up giving us Wi-Fi. Number \ntheory experiments from the 1970s gave us modern  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 331680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cryptography, which enables end to-end encryption, \nsecure online payments, and login. There are also  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337120,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "infamous things like GLP-1 drugs which trace \ndirectly back to government-f funded researchers  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "studying Gila monster venom. There are literally \nhundreds of these examples because we don't really  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fully know the applications of frontier research \nuntil we have done it. Nobody ever budgets for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352480,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the lizard spit economy. Neil deGrasse Tyson \nmay be best known as that famous science guy,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 357520,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but he is also a legitimate physicist who has \nrecently spoken about this trend in his field  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362000,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here on YouTube. His video actually came out as \nwe were writing this one and he has basically  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 367360,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "said the same thing which is probably worth more \nfrom someone with one foot still in the door of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371760,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "academia. So I will leave a link to that below. \nMore broadly though, other countries have seen all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 376880,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of this happening and they are capitalizing on our \ncomplacency by setting up grants and systems to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381760,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make it easier for these smart people to just make \nthe jump in the other direction. Some are even  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386640,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "specifically head-h hunting researchers, offering \nthem comparable salaries, fully funded labs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391200,
    "dDurationMs": 6560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and stable positions overseas. Canada launched a \n$ 1.7 billion Canadian program at the end of last  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397760,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year built to recruit more than a,000 worldleading \nresearchers, complete with money for their labs,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402720,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their equipment, and their grad students. The EU \nannounced a€ 500 million euro choose Europe for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 407520,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science package aimed at researchers looking \nfor the exit. And applications from US-based  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 412160,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "researchers from the European Research Council's \nmost prestigious grants went from 23 to 114 in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418080,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a single cycle. One university in the south of \nFrance even set up a program actually called Safe  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 422880,
    "dDurationMs": 6240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Place for Science. Subtle and got 298 applications \nfrom researchers in America, including people at  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429120,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stanford, Berkeley, and NASA. And of course, above \nall, China has been aggressively pursuing talent,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially amongst its own nationals who often \nstudy in the West and then stay in the West. For  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 439840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at least the last century, the USA has been by \nfar the largest hub of research and development  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444400,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funding anywhere in the world by some margin. But \nas of 2 years ago, adjusted for purchasing power  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450080,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "parody, China has now overtaken us, and they are \nnow channeling more resources into R\u0026D every year  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455440,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than we ever have. Uh, now a quick interlude here \nis that purchasing power parody accounts for the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 460800,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lower cost of most things in China. A million \ndollars in China just buys more equipment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "man-hour, and other resources than it does \nhere in America. Without that adjustment,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 469760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we are still technically throwing more money \nat R\u0026D. But in plain English, China is throwing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 474560,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more actual resources at upgrading their tech \ntree. Anyway, back to it. Today, there's a big  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "push to get a lot of the students that left \nChina to study in places like America to come  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483840,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "back to China along with all of the skills and \nexpertise they have gained from research and work  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488320,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at Western institutions. Often, this incentive is \nas simple as just a big pile of money. But again,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494400,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "more on those in a minute. The point is that \nif the brain drain trend that has served us  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498800,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the better part of a century actually \nreverses, that would be catastrophically bad.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504480,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Being at the cutting edge of a broad selection \nof sciences has been instrumental in America's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 508800,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outperforming economic growth and well our \nmilitary dominance over the same time period  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too. Competing in either metric without the \nfoundation of worldleading science is kind  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 518400,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of like trying to compete in AoE2 when your \nopponent is two ages ahead. It's going to go  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "badly. When scientists fled Germany in the 1930s \nand landed here, American patenting in the fields  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528240,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they joined jumped around a third. And the effect \nlasted well into the 1950s and arguably set us up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533280,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for our dominance over the next 50 years. But \nwell, the thing is, to be fair, none of this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538000,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is new. Countries from across the world have \nbeen well aware of brain train to America for a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long time. And they know how much it has helped \nkeep us at the forefront of most fields and how  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 548240,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much it has hurt their own development. They have \nalso always done what they can to get their smart  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 552800,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people back. But it's time to learn how many works \nto find out why they might finally be succeeding.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558240,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video is sponsored by Upside. Gas prices \nkeep climbing, groceries cost more every trip,  "
    } ]
  }, {
