    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can actually use deposited straight to your \nbank account. It's not points or credits that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 591680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expire and it stacks with whatever credit card \nrewards and loyalty programs you already have. So,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you're earning cash back on top of your cash back. \nChecking upside before I fill up has just become  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 601120,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "automatic for me. Upside has given back $1 billion \nto its users. To find out how much you could earn,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606480,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "download the free Upside app and use promo code \nhow money works to get an extra 25 cents back for  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 611280,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every gallon on your first tank of gas. That's an \nextra 25 cents back for every gallon on your first  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616240,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tank of gas using promo code how money works. \nScan the QR code on screen or click the link in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 621040,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the description to get started. Okay, so America \nhas stopped paying for a lot of the science that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 627440,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "doesn't pay for itself. But the second reason \nsmart people are leaving is a little bit more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 631920,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "personal. It's absolutely true that highly skilled \nprofessionals can earn more in the USA than they  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 637120,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "would typically be able to almost anywhere else \nin the world. But just because they can doesn't  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642000,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mean that there is a guarantee that they will. And \nlook, the frustrating part about this whole topic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that it is incredibly complicated. Even if we \nare just looking at their overall net economic  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652080,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "impact, a PhD student on a roughly $30,000 stipend \nmight end up contributing more to a country than  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 657920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a head-hunted AI researcher being offered a \n9-figure signing bonus. In typical research  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 662560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "roles, the compensation is not that great. The \naverages just get pulled up by the outliers that  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667520,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "get poached away into private industry, often in \nnarrow verticals that just happen to be jazzing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672080,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "investors at that point in time. Even a couple \nrungs up the ladder. The official NIH pay floor  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677120,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for a posttock is about $635,000 a year. Usually \nlocated in a city where that doesn't go very far.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684160,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The joke of a physicist going to work for Loheed \nMartin to pay off their student debt exists for a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688800,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reason. Physicists in the private sector earn \nroughly 30% more than the ones who stay in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693360,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "education. The defense and aerospace jobs pay even \nbetter still. And that's ignoring the people who  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698480,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just go and take a job as a quant on Wall Street. \nSo, you're a rocket scientist. How did you end up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704160,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here? It's all just numbers. Really, just changing \nwhat you're adding up. And to speak freely, the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 709600,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "money here is considerably more attractive. The \nproblem is that at these more basic income levels,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714400,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quality of life in America is statistically \nworse than in a lot of other countries around  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 718320,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the world. especially when the research mandates \nliving in high cost of living cities like Seattle,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 723200,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Boston, San Francisco, or DC. There is the \nclassic argument that even Mississippi or  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728240,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "state with the lowest GDP per capita mogs most \nmajor European economies on paper. But you  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733680,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can't eat productivity. And for people on average \nincomes, public transport, walkable cities, public  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 738880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "healthare, and just generally lower living costs \nmean they can normally afford a more comfortable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743520,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "life while pursuing their academic careers. And \nsince a lot of American academic talent moved  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747920,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the US in the first place to further their \nstudies and achieve a better quality of life,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are naturally more okay with moving abroad \nagain to continue the work and achieve a better  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 756800,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quality of life. This used to literally be our \nselling point to the best and brightest people  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 760880,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around the world. But other countries are just \nbecoming more competitive, especially in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765200,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fields we aren't really valuing. So yeah, it's \nnot great, but why is it happening now? Chasing  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770880,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "profit and unaffordable cities are not exactly \nnew American phenomena, but they have recently  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775600,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "been compounded by a gutting of scientific funding \nand a general push of anti-intellectualism. Last  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 781040,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "year's White House budget proposal called for \ncutting the National Institute of Health by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784800,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 40% and the National Science Foundation by \nmore than half. Congress ultimately rejected most  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790160,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of those cuts at the start of this year, but by \nthen a lot of the damage was already done. Between  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794960,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the hiring freezes, buyout offers, and great \nterminations, more than 15,000 people left federal  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 799920,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science agencies in 2025 alone. According to the \nAmerican Institute of Physics, the government's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805040,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "physical sciences workforce shrank by 12% in a \nsingle year, compared to 8% over the previous 26  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810720,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years combined. And that's before we even got to \nthe people entering the top of the talent pool.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 815920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tightened entry for high-end researchers \nand students coming from abroad has meant  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 819840,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "smaller classes and less funding and ultimately \nless manpower actually doing research. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825600,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "international student enrollment fell 17% last \nfall with graduate enrollment which is generally  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 830640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the people that actually staff research labs \nfalling by 12%. There is also something of a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 835680,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "soft power element in all of this as well. \nDoing research in America, getting an Ivy  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840080,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "League education, or building a startup in Silicon \nValley was for a long time seen as the goal by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 845040,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ambitious people from across the globe. Immigrant \nresearchers have won about 40% of America's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 850240,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "science Nobel prizes since the year 2000. Today, \nthat image still certainly exists, but it has been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 856400,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "uh tainted. And at the very least, a lot of people \nare now shopping around for alternatives. But all  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right, I know what you were saying. So what? A \nfew people are going to do non-economically viable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 867040,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "research somewhere else on someone else's dime. \nWho cares? At least we still have the profitable  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871680,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "research, right? Well, in a roundabout way, that \nprofit motive has actually started working against  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 877120,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "us. Researchers developing technology for dumb \nreasons like the good of humanity have long been  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882320,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "drawn to private institutions where they can make \nmuch more money. But their work is naturally more  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 886960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "closed off and focus more on developing products \nrather than building a foundation of scientific  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 891360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "understanding. This has been a trade-off forever \nwith graduate students picking between working  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 895680,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in industry and working in academia. Someone \nwith their PhD is every bit as susceptible to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 900480,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the cost of living pressures as anybody else and \narguably more so exposed to their student debt.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905440,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In many instances, it's to the point where the \nonly people that can afford to remain as career  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 909760,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "academics are people who have rich parents to fund \ntheir life. It's not great, but it gets worse. The  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916160,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "market opportunities have become so great that \neven tenured professors at high-end schools are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 920480,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "making the jump. The Atlantic reported more than \n80 current and former professors at schools like  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 925040,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Stanford, Maryland, and UT Austin have left or \ntaken leave to join OpenAI, Anthropic, Meta, and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930560,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Google DeepMind, including the chair of Berkeley's \nelectrical engineering and computer science  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 934560,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "department. As one Arizona State professor put it, \nI'm joining anthropic is the new meme right now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 940400,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which um isn't great, but it gets worse. This \nis ultimately even more resources going to push  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 946400,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this particular new technology forward within \nthese companies. But it also means that their  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 950480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "teaching isn't going to become accessible to \nnew students coming through these institutions.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954320,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Students that may in turn have developed something \ndifferent and potentially even more revolutionary.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 959120,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So even though this particular group hasn't \nactually left America, they have still kind  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of taken their brain power out of the American \necosystem, which means that they won't be around  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 967760,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to teach new students who could in turn build \nup a wider foundation of research. That might  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 972560,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be a great short-term deal for these companies, \nbut it's likely coming at the long-term cost of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 977120,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "wider progress in their respective fields. Now, I \nknow this all might sound a bit wishy-washy, but  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983520,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "developing scientific knowledge kind of depends \non a hierarchy of personnel. At the bottom are  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 988800,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "students learning how a field works, and in the \nmiddle is a group that may keep researching or may  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 993200,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "apply their learnings in industry. And at the very \ntop are the thought leaders at the cutting edge of  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 997520,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their particular branch of a discipline. They know \ntheir stuff usually after decades of research,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1002480,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "consulting, and advising other people up and \ndown this hierarchy. Today, we are losing a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1006640,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lot of the people entering at the bottom and \npitting away the people at the top into siloed  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1010560,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "institutions all while pricing out the people in \nthe middle. If we don't maintain it, this can also  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1015440,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very easily create a bad feedback loop. Colleges \ncan't offer courses, so top students look abroad,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1021200,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so there is less research getting done, so there \nis less funding coming in. So, more professors  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1025920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "start looking for work abroad, too. add less \nmoney for entire fields on top of this and  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1030560,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it really could get pretty bad. The good news is \nthat so far we are still pretty early on in this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1035680,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "process. Most people anywhere on Earth would still \nhappily take a place at a university like MIT.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1041520,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the trend is not our friend and these fields \nnaturally compound on themselves. But this also  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1047440,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "raises a pretty fair question. Is this actually a \nproblem? Sure, we have attracted a lot of talent  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1053040,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at every level of this pyramid from overseas for \na long time. But we also have a lot of very smart  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1058160,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "people right here at home. The acceptance rates at \ntop colleges, research firms, grants, and jobs in  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1063120,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these fields are legendarily slim. And sometimes \nthe difference between the average smart person  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1068160,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a worldleading researcher is just getting the \nopportunity to do the research in the first place.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1073040,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If countries like China really are investing \nserious money into taking back top talent,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1077040,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there is a reasonable argument that giving these \nslots to international students has effectively  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1081120,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "disenfranchised an almost as good American \nhopeful. all to train people who may end up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1086080,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "furthering the scientific ambitions of an economic \nand potentially militaristic rival. It's a not  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1091520,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unreasonable concern that is made worse by the \nalready existing trend of reversing brain drain.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1096880,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, it's easy to get a little bit conspiratorial \nhere and assume that they are sending over spies  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1101440,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to steal our intellectual property. And well, \nin certain cases, that does happen. But the much  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1106560,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "larger problem is also much more simple. In the \npast, the vast majority of purely self-interested  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1111760,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "STEM graduates from almost all countries in the \nworld would choose to stay and work in America  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1116400,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because of, well, the opportunities, the quality \nof life, and the extra money that I've spent half  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1121360,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this video yapping about. This was especially true \nfor students coming from developing countries. But  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1126880,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now, fewer are staying. From China, in particular, \naround 90% of their STEM PhD graduates used to  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1133520,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "still be living and working in America years \nafter finishing their degrees. But today,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1137760,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "according to the National Science Foundation's \nmost recent tracking, that is down to just 76%.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1143840,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, obviously, that is still a majority. But it \nalso means that the share leaving has jumped by  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1149120,
    "dDurationMs": 6080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "about 140%. On top of all of the self-inflicted \nheadwinds we have put on this trend, China is  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1155200,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pouring money into facilitating the reversal. \nIts flagship recruitment effort, a program it  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1160160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has never officially announced, reportedly offers \nreturning researchers signing bonuses that can  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1164560,
    "dDurationMs": 6640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "reach $700,000 plus help buying a home. So even in \nthe complete absence of any sinister intentions,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1171200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "normal students just following the best available \nopportunities for themselves could easily end up  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1175760,
    "dDurationMs": 6400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on this path. And this is genuinely causing some \nbig hits. The founder of Moonshot AI, Yong Jerene,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1182160,
    "dDurationMs": 5920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got his PhD at Carnegie Melon. And well, his Kimmy \nmodels are kind of moonshotting our domestic AIs  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1188080,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the moment, which even though we may not like \nit, is a major component of our economy. Now, it's  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1193280,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "happening outside of AI, too. The mathematician \nJangi Tong, famous for a landmark proof about the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1199040,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gaps between prime numbers, left UC Santa Barbara \nlast year for a university in Guanghou. Now,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1204320,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I really can't tell you what the right answer is \nhere. And for every argument about furthering a  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1208480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rival science, there is a counter-argument about \ninternational students overcontributing to the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1212560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "funding of these educational institutions in the \nfirst place. They poured about $43 billion into  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1217360,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the US economy last year alone. But genuinely, I'd \nbe interested to see your guys' thoughts in the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1222080,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comments. I can't see that going badly. For what \nit's worth, if this really is an adversarial zero  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1227920,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sum game, then well, we are still taking more \nsmart people from them than they are from us.  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1233200,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's more is that if we really wanted \nto avoid this dilemma in the first place,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1236720,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we should probably double down on K through2 \neducation for the domestic talent pipeline,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1240880,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but that's a whole different video. The point is \non either side of this debate, we should probably  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1245520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be trying really hard to reduce the exodus of \nthe talent that is already here. This is also,  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1250560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let's be honest, a very emotional argument where \nit's all too easy to dismiss one side as racist  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1255520,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for raising legitimate concerns, and it's also \nvery easy for actual racist ideas to piggyback  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1260560,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on some valid criticism. The unfortunate reality \nis that companies know this and they know the  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1266080,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "emotions of this debate will make for a great \nget out of jail free card. So go watch this  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1270480,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "video next to find out why the fear of China \nhas become such an effective tool for the AI  "
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 1274560,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "industry specifically. And don't forget to like \nand subscribe to keep on learning how money works."
    } ]
  } ]
}
